# =============================================================================
# jyyj-mcp 助手 - repository ignore rules
# =============================================================================
# The tracked content of this repository is: the patched source tree under
# mcp-server-excel/, the local build/release tooling (build.sh, release.sh, tools/),
# and the deployment/verification notes (*.md). Everything below is either a local
# toolchain cache, a build output, or a probe artefact, so none of it belongs in git.
#
# The nested mcp-server-excel/.gitignore still applies to that subtree and wins for
# any pattern both files define (git evaluates rules from the top down, deepest last).
# =============================================================================

# --- Pinned SDK and package caches (multi-GB, machine specific) --------------
.dotnet10/
.dotnet-home/
.nuget-packages/

# --- Build output and published artefacts ------------------------------------
# excel-mcp-bin/ is the deploy directory the local MCP client points at; it holds
# ~135 copied assemblies that are rebuilt from source, never edited by hand.
excel-mcp-bin/
dist/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/

# --- Agent workspace (local memory / session state, not project source) ------
.workbuddy/

# --- Probe, demo and regression artefacts ------------------------------------
_demo/
_regshards/
_trash/
_research/

# --- Publish staging tree (tools/publish.py) ---------------------------------
# A standalone clone of the publishable file set, with its own .git. It lives inside the
# workspace so the whole workflow stays in one place, and is never part of what gets published.
_publish/

# --- Run logs and ad-hoc listings --------------------------------------------
_*.log
*.log
_*.txt

# --- Upstream CI workflows (excluded deliberately) ---------------------------
# These 11 workflows target the upstream maintainer's infrastructure: self-hosted
# Windows runners with Excel installed, sealed release secrets, and gh-pages /
# plugin-marketplace deploy targets that do not exist here. Included unchanged they
# would fail on every push and mail a failure notice to the repository owner, so
# they are withheld rather than shipped broken. The definitions remain available
# upstream at https://github.com/sbroenne/mcp-server-excel/tree/main/.github/workflows
mcp-server-excel/.github/workflows/

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
